WEBVTT

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.110
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:38.530
Just to make sure,
this isn't a lovers' suicide, right?

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.440
N-No!

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.480
Good.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.150
Ango Sakaguchi.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:49.480
No, it would be best to call him
a nameless bandit now.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:54.280
What I wanted tonight was this woman's head.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.280
I have no interest in you.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.480
I see.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.860
So let's call it a tie, then.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.360
Wait, Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.860
Wait, Ango!

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.360
Ango!

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.390
"Episode 3"

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.610
"In the Forest of the Cherry Blossoms,
Beneath the Full Bloom."

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.860
Ango Sakaguchi's most famous work,

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:53.070
noted for the way in which
the beautiful depictions of the scenery and

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.730
the gruesome events it describes
enhance one another.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.280
The fact that it lets the reader
decide for themselves

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.730
the answer is probably part of it, too.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:04.190
Everyone has their own different interpretation.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:09.570
So the great Shimazaki- <i>sensei</i>
has his own interpretation?

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.860
I'd love to hear it.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.610
Well...

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:15.190
As I see it,

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:18.730
the bandit, who's the story's protagonist...

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:40.980
Broke bastard.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:43.070
He had nothing worth taking.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.820
Some country bumpkin.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:50.650
I think he was satisfied with his life.

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:54.860
He had everything he could want
up there in the mountains.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:57.150
He never ran out of food.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.570
If he wanted something to drink,
he could just steal it.

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:09.730
Anyone who passed through
the forests and mountains was his prey.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.280
But...

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.030
Even a man like him had one thing he feared.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:33.940
For some reason, the cherry blossom trees
in the forest terrified him.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:38.610
He didn't know why, but he knew
he'd find the answer someday,

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:43.610
and so he told himself it didn't concern him.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:49.440
And then one day...

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.480
He met the woman.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:10.030
She was a beautiful woman.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:27.320
You're my wife now.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:35.570
The man thought to himself he was willing
to do whatever the woman wanted him to.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:39.980
The woman, huh?

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:44.440
For a man who lived his whole life
never knowing want,

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:50.400
this may have been his first connection
with another person.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.030
And that's why he became her puppet.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:57.280
Even after getting a glimpse of her true nature.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:02.530
The woman wanted to live in the capital.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.690
Kill them.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.440
Will this do?

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.940
Yes. It will.

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:33.690
This is very good.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.650
Good, very good.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.440
You look so friendly.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.280
You're a wonderful couple.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:51.940
But you'd be lonely if it were
just the two of you.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:55.320
I know! I've got the perfect idea.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:57.730
Let's do that.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:02.360
Honey, bring me more heads!

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.900
Heads?

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.480
If there're lots of heads here,
nobody will be lonely!

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:11.480
It'll be so lively here, too!

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:13.570
Won't it be wonderful?

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:21.980
And so the man wandered the capital
in search of heads to sever

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:24.030
to fulfill the woman's desires.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:28.070
A sad and terrifying story.

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:31.230
Terrifying? Hah!

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:34.110
That book's nothing but an ideal.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:35.110
An ideal?

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:36.730
Yup.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:39.980
Ango's ideal way of life.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.900
That's the only way I can read it.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:51.110
Welcome back.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:53.280
Will this do?

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:55.070
Yes.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.230
Wonderful.

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:59.360
Such a pretty face the man has, right?

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:03.730
So he needs a pretty daughter.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:08.150
The two will live happily.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.940
And then one day, they'll be drawn together,

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:13.820
and find themselves in the throes
of passionate love.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.610
Love is wonderful.

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:20.530
Sometimes it's hatred, sometimes anger,
sometimes it's lies...

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:25.070
All of that happens, but it's all for love.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:30.570
And with that love, any obstacle
just becomes fuel for your passion.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.570
How wonderful...

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:38.480
But the flames of passionate love
can bring wicked things, too.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:42.030
I'm jealous!

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:45.820
Why do you have all the luck? Damn it!

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:49.650
The man died, painfully.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:52.980
Tell me. How long will we be doing this?

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.150
What do you mean "how long"?

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:57.230
That's a strange thing to say.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:09:00.980
Every day I bring you new heads to play with.

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:03.280
I don't understand why.

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:05.650
Then why don't you try it?

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:07.190
I...

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.070
I'm sick of this.

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:13.230
What? Did you get scared?

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:15.980
When did you get so weak?

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.730
I'm not weak.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:19.480
That's not it...

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:22.440
If you're not weak, what are you?

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:24.360
I hate the fact that there's no end!

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:27.400
Now you're making even less sense.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:30.400
Life has no end.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.610
Every day you eat.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:35.280
Every day you sleep.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.190
No end, right?

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:40.610
That's different than playing
with someone's head!

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.280
Traitor!

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:48.440
You can't stay here, then!

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.400
You can't stay in the capital.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:52.610
Will you go back to the mountain?

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.230
The mountain?

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:57.150
Of course, I'll go with you.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.480
Together we'll live in the mountains. And then...

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:07.980
No!

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:10.860
We can't go back!

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:16.280
I'm staying here!

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.860
Staying here with you forever!

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.110
So don't go!

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:23.730
Don't leave me alone!

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:26.110
Of course.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:28.320
I won't go anywhere.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:34.110
I see.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.940
What the hell is he doing?

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.570
Where are you going?

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:42.570
To defeat that woman and wake up Ango!

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:46.980
Right now, he's Ango Sakaguchi,
but he's not Ango Sakaguchi.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:48.940
He's just a bandit.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:51.190
You saw it too, right?

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:52.980
That woman's insane!

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.190
He can't stay with her!

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:59.030
But right now, that's what he wants.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:04.230
In the original book, the bandit
gets sick of living with the woman,

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:06.400
and tries to go back to the mountains.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:10.650
But right now, he's afraid of going back.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:14.280
As if he knows what happens if he does.

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.860
What happens if he does?

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:21.110
You're his friend and you didn't read his book?

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:25.860
I'm sure I did, but... I just can't remember.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:28.360
Let's get the story moving.

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:30.530
Give it a kick in the butt.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:38.860
I don't understand
the attraction of the capital.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:40.900
What are they talking about?

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:43.110
What is there to say?

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:45.940
There's nothing I want to say.

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:55.360
You bastard!

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:01.030
Sorry, we're going to borrow her.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:04.610
If you want her back, come to us.

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:07.650
We'll be waiting under the cherry tree.

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:15.070
You almost killed me, so...

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:18.860
Now we're even.

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:25.440
Is it just me, or are we the bad guys here?

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:29.030
Did you think you were a good person?

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:34.530
Why do I have to stand watch too?

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:37.730
Hey, Saku Oda! Saku Oda!

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.150
Saku Oda--

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.150
What are you doing?

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:48.030
Oh, is that you, Chuya- <i>kun</i> ?

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.900
You found me, huh?

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:54.900
You don't intend to delve like that, do you?

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:56.780
I have to go...

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:59.480
My friend is suffering inside that book...

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:04.820
Chuya- <i>kun</i> ?

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:06.690
Look, what do you want me to do?

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:08.440
I can't go myself.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:10.530
Why can't I go in?

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:12.980
I'm gonna kick Ango's ass later.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:20.110
It's probably Dazai- <i>kun</i> 's and my fault
that he's trapped in there.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:28.110
Now, a toast to the success of
the Modern Literature Discussion Group!

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.320
What do you mean, "success"?

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:33.190
Saku Oda's two hours late!

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:34.820
Sorry, sorry.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:38.820
But you were both drunk
off your asses when I got here!

00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:40.780
So we're even.

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:43.230
Yeah, right.

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:47.230
Gah, I've got so much more to say!

00:13:47.230 --> 00:13:50.360
That's enough insulting Shiga- <i>sensei</i> .

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:52.980
That guy's got ears everywhere!

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:56.690
Who cares?
Insults are the beginning of corruption.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.230
There we go! Ango's gonna
tell us about corruption again.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.900
Again?

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.730
You like Shiga- <i>sensei</i> .

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:07.360
Yeah. I've got nothing against Shiga.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:11.360
But if Dazai wants to insult him,
I'm not going to stop him.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:13.030
'Cause it's fun to listen to!

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:14.360
Yup!

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:17.480
A man who's pure of heart is boring.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:19.360
Men become interesting after they fall.

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:23.860
Well, I won't deny that the true nature
of man can be found there.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:27.690
Listen to this, I came up with
an idea for a new story!

00:14:27.690 --> 00:14:29.900
What? Tell me about it!

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:31.900
The hero's a bandit.

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:35.110
Someone who's fallen as far as he can go!

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:39.280
He lives in the mountains, killing as he likes,
and wanting for nothing.

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:41.110
What a jerk!

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:45.860
But he's satisfied with his life.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:47.400
Do you know why?

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.900
Because his life is all he knows.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:50.780
Correct.

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:54.150
He's spent his whole life in the mountains!

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:56.900
He's never been bothered by it.

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:58.900
Doesn't that seem cool?

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:01.650
But wouldn't he be lonely by himself?

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:06.360
If he was always alone,
he wouldn't know what "lonely" meant.

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:07.940
Wow, he'd be invincible!

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:11.690
Yeah. Invincible, in a sense.
Perfect, and complete.

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:15.030
But then one day he meets a woman,

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:17.900
and shockingly, falls in love with her.

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:19.190
What do you think happens?

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:21.190
He stops being invincible.

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:22.030
Yes!

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:23.820
When you fall in love and live with someone,

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.530
sometimes you'll have trouble with
the fact that you have different values.

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.570
You may want your distance.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:33.070
But love is like the truth
of nature of the heart.

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:37.860
Once you've fallen, you're not going back.

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:42.110
So what does that man do if the woman dies?

00:15:42.110 --> 00:15:46.070
He falls into loneliness
for the first time in his life.

00:15:46.070 --> 00:15:48.110
Great ending, right?

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:51.690
Ango tried to depict a man's fall.

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:53.480
He wanted to be that man.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.980
He wanted to complete his aesthetics.

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.150
But now he's...

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:04.110
What is this scary woman?

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:06.530
Just a normal human.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:07.610
She is?

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:12.610
People can't accept someone whose values
are too different than their own.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:18.820
Sometimes that person will seem
to be something inhuman.

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:20.820
You're Delvers, aren't you?

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:24.610
Her disgusting hobbies may
make her seem less like a woman,

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:27.730
and more like a monster.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.530
To him, and to us.

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:42.610
So she was the Taint?

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:10.780
He's finally here...

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:14.110
Ango?

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:18.570
I can't lose her! I...!

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:24.030
I don't want to be alone!

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:25.730
My love!

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:29.070
You make me so happy!

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:32.570
I couldn't live without you either...

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:36.400
So... protect me!

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:39.940
Ango Sakaguchi!

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:45.650
In this story, the woman becomes a monster
and the man kills her himself!

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:46.730
So...

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.190
You have to be the one to defeat her!

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.780
Ango Sakaguchi.

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:02.110
Yes. That's my name.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:04.530
I...

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:13.190
Ango!

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:14.780
I know.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.900
It's my own book!

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:19.900
In the end, the bandit kills the woman,

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:22.820
and dies knowing true loneliness.

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:26.690
Such is the beautiful life of a fallen man.

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:29.360
But now, I...

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:32.530
I'm scared of loneliness!

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:38.230
Saku Oda and Dazai both left me!

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:42.610
Just two years after
we drank together that night!

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:44.860
So I don't...

00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:48.150
...want to lose anymore!

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:51.730
What are you talking about?

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.230
You're a storyteller, right?

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:57.150
So don't fear loneliness!

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:07.940
Saku Oda!

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:11.110
Looks like I made it in time for my big scene.

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:12.610
Ango!

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:15.110
The Ango Sakaguchi I know is a show-off,

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:19.320
but he keeps showing off until the very end!

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:23.650
That's right.

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:25.570
You don't need to tell me.

00:19:27.150 --> 00:19:31.280
Don't fear loneliness. Don't fear the fall.

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:32.320
I...

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:45.030
I am going to be a great storyteller!

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:46.370
"Ango Sakaguchi"

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:49.480
What are you doing?

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:52.730
You promised we'd always be together!

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:54.320
If you kill me...!

00:19:58.320 --> 00:19:59.440
Shut up.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:22.360
These beautiful cherry blossoms
will become the light that illuminates me.

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:27.610
And then I'll see that
there's nothing around me.

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:31.860
I'll understand that I'm lonely.

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:35.530
Come on, don't die before I do.

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:37.570
You'll make me sad.

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:46.030
This is the proper ending for this story.

00:20:50.610 --> 00:20:51.650
Sheesh.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:54.860
You took too long.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:03.400
What are you doing here, Chuya?

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:08.440
I came to laugh at peach flower boy
when he came back with his ass kicked!

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:09.730
So mean!

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:11.070
And while I'm at it...

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:19.400
Hey.

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:22.230
You showed up, huh?

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:23.610
So it seems.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:30.650
Yes. Looks like another success.

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:34.780
Ango Sakaguchi will come to aid us, too.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.530
I'm curious, too.

00:21:40.530 --> 00:21:44.190
I can understand why Dazai and Oda
were called into Sakaguchi's book.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:45.530
But him?

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:46.650
Yes.

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:52.030
He may hold the key to this battle.

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:57.920
"In the Forest of the Cherry Blossoms,
Beneath the Full Bloom"
"Part 2"

00:23:28.360 --> 00:23:30.110
Literary Gourmet!

00:23:28.460 --> 00:23:32.280
"Ango's Hot Pot in My Memories!"

00:23:30.110 --> 00:23:32.280
The Monkfish Hot Pot in My Memories!

00:23:32.820 --> 00:23:37.320
I'm really... hungry.

00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:39.400
What's going on? It's pitch black!

00:23:39.400 --> 00:23:41.570
I made you a stew!

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:42.150
"Bubble bubble"

00:23:41.570 --> 00:23:43.650
No! I can't tell what's in it!

00:23:43.650 --> 00:23:44.650
Eat it!

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:45.520
"NOM!"

00:23:45.530 --> 00:23:47.860
"Gwaah!"

00:23:45.530 --> 00:23:47.780
Dazai- <i>kun</i> , what's wrong? Dazai- <i>kun</i> !

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:48.360
"Flip"

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:50.030
It's good...

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:54.160
"Monkfish Hot Pot"
"A stew that uses every part of a high-quality monkfish.
Originally a dish made in Ibaraki."

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:51.690
The soft, tender liver is delicious!

00:23:51.690 --> 00:23:54.280
And the seasonal vegetables
pair perfectly with the meat of the fish!

00:23:54.280 --> 00:23:56.280
It's going inside my friend's mouth.

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:58.530
I couldn't make something bad, could I?

00:23:58.530 --> 00:23:59.780
Ango!
